  "claims": {
    "normal_path": "Finalize calls the relationship upsert twice, tag 1 then tag 2, passing the same container descriptor through r13. The retained interval has no conditional branch or return between the calls. The earlier PR #2126 maps the selected writes and their normal meanings.",
    "exception_path": "Finalize and its action wrapper have no LSDA. The exact dispatch and parent call-site rows have no landing pad or action. The relationship upsert has two local cleanup pads, both for representation-conversion iterator calls; PR #4288 verifies that each publishes the computed representation fields and resumes unwinding rather than restoring the old descriptor.",
    "interpretation": "If an exception propagates from the second upsert, the inspected frames contain no local rollback for the first upsert. The evidence supports a potentially partially mutated in-memory map, not atomic rollback.",
    "limits": "This does not establish that a particular exception occurs, allocator behavior, outer transaction handling, state persistence, process survival, or any catch/rollback above the inspected parent caller."
